<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pōmare I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1743–1803</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pōmare I, born Tū, was a Tahitian chief who founded the Pōmare dynasty and the Kingdom of Tahiti. Using <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/musket">muskets</a> obtained from visiting ships and the help of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hms-bounty">Bounty</a> mutineers, he extended his power over Tahiti and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moorea">Moorea</a> from about 1788. He handed the title to his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pomare-ii">Pōmare II</a> in 1791 but remained influential until his death in 1803.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pomare-i.jpg" alt="Pōmare I" width="320" height="414" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: John Webber · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:John_Webber%27s_oil_painting_of_Otoo,_1777_(restored).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
